{
  "about": "The W over P rows of the pico ABI performance matrix measured on Windows x64 (docs/pico-perf-matrix.md section 6): arm W the library of the Windows package, arm P zenoh-pico built with MSVC as the same build, run by scripts/host-bench/windows/perf_matrix.ps1 and judged by `scripts/host-bench/perf_matrix.py --gate` on the reading it writes. The rows, their four shapes and the rule are those of deploy/pico_perf_ceiling.json; `platform` keeps the two apart, so a run is judged only against the rows of the platform it was made on, and `stdlib` (`nostd`, the package a release ships) against the rows of the library it measured. A row is written only from the gate's own output for a run, never by hand.",
